 Elsa Rockefeller, church, historic marker, and headstones in original burial ground in Somerset County, New Jersey.</p></scopecontent></c><c id="4dbc252ec2866672f576ae64c5dd5ac5" level="file"><did><unittitle>Germantown, New York - Simon Rockefeller Home</unittitle><unitid type="aspace_uri">/repositories/2/archival_objects/1292646</unitid><unitdate calendar="gregorian" datechar="creation" era="ce" normal="1930/1930">1930</unitdate><physdesc id="a5b04bf52c995570d45e778ed3746349">2 prints</physdesc><container altrender="Half Letter Document Box" id="3e68cf7cc47f524097ba826ada7cad40" label="Still Image [A0000000105900]" type="box">1</container><container id="b93b702b0a2019959b54976569fbd707" parent="3e68cf7cc47f524097ba826ada7cad40" type="folder">3</container></did><scopecontent id="a993eea8bc1857b77a63b9edbe3c9d8b"><head>Scope and Contents</head><p>Exterior photographs of home of Simon Rockefeller (born in Germany 1730, died in Germantown, New York 1795) where three generations of Rockefellers were born.</p></scopecontent></c><c id="e313437c004321f238f6562942472ff0" level="file"><did><unittitle>Tucker Place, Godfrey-Lucy Rockefeller House, Michigan Hill, New York</unittitle><unitid type="aspace_uri">/repositories/2/archival_objects/1292647</unitid><unitdate calendar="gregorian" datechar="creation" era="ce">undated</unitdate><physdesc id="aa8de43469891b03ca725df89c527bf5">1 print</physdesc><container altrender="Half Letter Document Box" id="23e27a33a6d334eb23013d76e78693e5" label="Still Image [A0000000105900]" type="box">1</container><container id="c216d078e3c1875e82ace243197e4085" parent="23e27a33a6d334eb23013d76e78693e5" type="folder">4</container></did></c><c id="c14665ca57b32a879d90e4f07d702f78" level="file"><did><unittitle>Portrait - Egbert Rockefeller</unittitle><unitid type="aspace_uri">/repositories/2/archival_objects/1292648</unitid><unitdate calendar="gregorian" datechar="creation" era="ce">undated</unitdate><container altrender="Half Letter Document Box" id=